Esp32Tap Rev E liveness switch worst-case corners (Q3, D8, C22, C23, R34, R35 over tolerance, temperature, supply)
* ASSUMPTIONS:
* Every number below that is not quoted from a data sheet is an assumption
* of this deck. Corner values were found by an extreme-point search (every
* combination of the low/high end of f, duty, R34, R35, C22 and C23 with the
* diode, driver and threshold fixed for the temperature), and the combination
* that was worst for the question is the one written here.
*
* Supply and pin: 3.0...3.6 V. The weak-driver corner is VDD=3.0 V with the
* pin high at VDD-0.4 = 2.6 V and low at 0.4 V. The strong corner is 3.6 V
* rail to rail. A pin that does not reach the rails shrinks the pump swing from
* 3.0 V to 2.2 V.
* Capacitors (assumed totals, not measured; Samsung curves could not be fetched):
*   C22 100 nF X7R 50 V 0603: +/-10 % tolerance, +/-15 % X7R temperature, -5 %
*   DC bias at 3.3 V, -3 % ageing -> 70.5 nF low (0.9*0.85*0.95*0.97), 126.5 nF
*   high (1.1*1.15, no bias or ageing credit).
*   C23 1 uF X5R 50 V 0603 (CL10A105KB8NNNC class): +/-10 %, +/-15 % X5R temperature,
*   -25 % DC bias at 2.5 V (0603 1 uF at 50 V rating is bias-sensitive; assumed),
*   -3 % ageing -> 0.557 uF low in steady state (0.9*0.85*0.75*0.97), 1.265 uF high
*   (1.1*1.15). From rest the gate sits near 0 V, so the D corners use 0.742 uF
*   (the same without the bias term). During pickup and release the bias loss
*   varies with the gate voltage; the high value assumes none, which bounds release.
* R34, R35 +/-1 %. Pulse frequency 950...1050 Hz, duty 40...60 %, 1 us edges.
* Q3 AO3400A (Alpha and Omega, Rev 3.1): Vgs(th) 0.65...1.45 V at 25 C, 250 uA;
* Ciss 630 pF typ; Igss 100 nA max at 12 V. Q3 gate parasitics are in every
* pump as a 630 pF capacitor and a 26 Mohm resistor (100 nA at 2.6 V, pessimistic
* because Igss is rated at 12 V). Threshold temperature coefficient: -3 mV/C
* (assumption; data sheet Fig 2 shows the 125 C curve about 0.2 V left of 25 C,
* about -2 mV/C). So the highest threshold is 1.585 V at -20 C, 1.45 V at 25 C,
* 1.315 V at 70 C; the lowest is 0.515 V at 70 C and 0.65 V at 25 C.
* Q3 model: ESP_Q3 conducts fully only from VT+0.5 V and the coil loop shows
* 21 mA the moment the gate passes VT. A real AO3400A needs roughly VT+0.2 V
* for 21 mA (data sheet Fig 2), so crossing VT here is optimistic for turn-on
* and conservative for release; the 0.5 V margin below is the model's own
* full-on point and is the requirement used for the steady gate.
* D8 BAT54S (Nexperia data sheet unreachable: HTTP 403 for this client). The
* Diodes Incorporated BAT54/A/C/S data sheet DS11005 Rev 35-2, same device
* class, supplies the points; the typical Vf values were read by eye from its
* Fig 1 and are approximate: Vf at 0.1 mA / 1 mA: -20 C 0.31/0.37 V (between its
* -40 C and 0 C curves), 25 C 0.22/0.31 V, 70 C 0.15/0.21 V. Table limits at
* 25 C: Vf <= 0.24 V at 0.1 mA, <= 0.32 V at 1 mA, <= 0.40 V at 10 mA;
* IR <= 2.0 uA at VR=25 V. Fig 2 typical reverse current at about 3 V:
* 0.06 uA at 25 C, 2.1 uA at 75 C, about 0.005 uA at -20 C (extrapolated).
* Weak diodes add 20 mV to the typical Vf, strong diodes subtract 20 mV
* (part-to-part spread; assumption). Diode Is and N are fitted to hit the two
* Vf points with Rs=4 ohm; N absorbs the junction temperature because the
* simulator stays at 27 C. Reverse leakage is a separate smooth current
* source, because an ideal diode's saturation current cannot carry it.
* Reverse leakage at hot: 2.5 uA is the typical figure rounded up. The
* HOTX corner uses 15 uA = 2.0 uA (25 C max, 25 V) * 0.3 (3 V against 25 V,
* Fig 2) * 25 (25 -> 70 C on the typical curve, 35 at 75 C), a bound that
* assumes a part at its maximum leakage at temperature.
* Coil: K1 237 ohm, 0.5 H, 5.0 V, Q1 saturated; D4 clamp as relay_drive_release.
* Pickup and release are measured as the gate crossing the stated Q3 threshold.
* Requirements (limits come from these, not from the results):
*   A steady gate >= highest threshold + 0.5 V at the same temperature.
*   B pickup (first edge to highest threshold) <= 15 ms, half the 30 ms firmware
*     precharge; failing the 30 ms precharge itself is worse.
*   C release: no limit of its own; existing test bound 0.2 s on the nominal figure.
*   D one stray edge or a pin that steps and stays: peak <= lowest threshold
*     (hot, 0.515 V) - 0.1 V = 0.415 V.
* Where a corner fails a requirement its assertion is a bracket around what
* the model gives, labelled FAILS in assertions.json and sim/README.md.
* NON-CLAIMS:
* Not measured. Simple models: a smooth-conductance Q3, fitted two-point
* diodes, ideal capacitors with assumed derating, an ideal pin source. Relay
* contact motion, release time and bounce are not modeled. Stacked worst cases
* are pessimistic by construction and may be far rarer than any one part; the
* Monte Carlo in run_montecarlo.py shows how rare. Capacitor derating and
* the Q3 temperature coefficient are assumptions; the Samsung curve and the
* AO3400A Vth-versus-temperature curve were not obtained.

.include models/behavioral.inc

* Diode models, one per corner kind, with the reverse leakage on each junction.
* COLD: -20 C, Vf typical+20 mV, leakage typical; Vf 0.33 V @0.1 mA, 0.39 V @1 mA; IL 0.003 uA
.model D8_COLD D(Is=1.432e-10 N=0.9475 Rs=4 Cjo=10p)
.subckt PUMPX_COLD pin gate params: R35=560 R34=100k C22=100n C23=1u IL=1u
R35 pin pump_in {R35}
C22 pump_in pump_ac {C22}
D8A 0 pump_ac D8_COLD
BLA 0 pump_ac I={-IL*0.5*(1+tanh((v(pump_ac)-v(0))/0.05))}
D8B pump_ac gate D8_COLD
BLB pump_ac gate I={-IL*0.5*(1+tanh((v(gate)-v(pump_ac))/0.05))}
C23 gate 0 {C23}
R34 gate 0 {R34}
.ends

* ROOM: 25 C, Vf typical+20 mV, leakage typical; Vf 0.24 V @0.1 mA, 0.33 V @1 mA; IL 0.07 uA
.model D8_ROOM D(Is=1.686e-07 N=1.451 Rs=4 Cjo=10p)
.subckt PUMPX_ROOM pin gate params: R35=560 R34=100k C22=100n C23=1u IL=1u
R35 pin pump_in {R35}
C22 pump_in pump_ac {C22}
D8A 0 pump_ac D8_ROOM
BLA 0 pump_ac I={-IL*0.5*(1+tanh((v(pump_ac)-v(0))/0.05))}
D8B pump_ac gate D8_ROOM
BLB pump_ac gate I={-IL*0.5*(1+tanh((v(gate)-v(pump_ac))/0.05))}
C23 gate 0 {C23}
R34 gate 0 {R34}
.ends

